   "text": {
    "L1": "In the poem, a child wishes to be different workers. Each worker has something the child likes.",
    "L2": "The fruit-seller sings along the lane, and the gardener digs and never hurries.",
    "L3": "The watchman uses his lantern and keeps away our worries. His work helps keep us safe.",
    "L4": "The poem teaches us to respect every kind of work. No honest job is small or less important.",
    "L5": "When we describe a person, we use who. This is the potter who makes clay pots.",
    "L6": "Use an article before a job: my mother is a teacher, and he is an electrician.",
    "L7": "Now make a wish line: I wish I were the worker who does a useful job."
   },
